.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
DBUS IPC module for evidence. 

this implements a service (with defined messages), but can be changed into a generic filter with little effort.
.PP
tested with DBUS 0.12 -- deprecated
.PP
by Azundris
.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "static DBusHandlerResult client_sent (DBusMessageHandler * handler, DBusConnection * connection, DBusMessage * message, void * user_data)\fC [static]\fP"
.PP
callback: DBUS sent us stuff 
.PP
\fBReturns:\fP
.RS 4
DBUS_HANDLER_RESULT_ALLOW_MORE_HANDLERS 
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIhandler\fP the handle of this DBUS-handler 
.br
\fIconnection\fP the connection 
.br
\fImessage\fP the message we were sent 
.br
\fIuser_data\fP &connection (in case we need to call \fBipc_module_exit()\fP)
.RE
.PP

.SS "static void dispatch_status (DBusConnection * connection, DBusDispatchStatus status, void * data)\fC [static]\fP"
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIconnection\fP the connection on which the dispatch-status changed 
.br
\fIstatus\fP the new status 
.br
\fIdata\fP unused If the dispatch status is DBUS_DISPATCH_DATA_REMAINS, then dbus_connection_dispatch() needs to be called to process incoming messages, BUT NOT from inside this function! It should simply set flag indicating that messages should be dispatched in the next iteration of the main-loop. http://freedesktop.org/Software/dbus/doc/api/html/group__DBusConnection.html#a39
.RE
.PP

.SS "static DBusHandlerResult handle_cmd (DBusConnection * connection, DBusMessage * message, char * m)\fC [static]\fP"
.PP
call a command (ls, file-info, . 
.PP
..) within evidence 
.PP
\fBReturns:\fP
.RS 4
the result of any of the reply_*() functions (DBUS_HANDLER_RESULT_ALLOW_MORE_HANDLERS) 
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIconnection\fP the connection the request was sent on 
.br
\fImessage\fP the request 
.br
\fIm\fP the sub-command ('minor')
.RE
.PP

